      "message": "Thanks this is a really interesting investigation!\n\nI made notes about known issues, gaps etc.\n- easy: missing feature of spirv-reader\n- no combined image samplers in WGSL, but also none in HLSL\n- uniformity errors. We\u0027re designing an opt-out that spirv-reader will generate. This is mainly arguing at standards committee now.\n- WGSL requires vertex shaders to have a \u0027position\u0027 output.  At least one sample here breaks.\n\nGenerally it looks like Tint\u0027s output is more chatty and harder to read.",
