      "writtenOn": "2022-11-25T18:46:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WGSL has a conservative uniformity analysis to try to protect developers from ill-defined derivatives and anisotropic filtering.\n\nI\u0027d be interested in seeing the original SkSL that led to this, to see if this catches a real bug or if the analysis is too conservative.\n\nWe\u0027re designing an opt-out of this analysis, to support Unity and others.\nhttps://github.com/gpuweb/gpuweb/issues/3554\n\nThe spirv-reader will at least have a knob to opt-out, or opt-out by default.",
      "revId": "ee448f4fdcc0c2d58d42dd964ebf3a179c9d298a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
